Speaker 1: Some games, you have to figure out a solution and execute with timing, but then there's games where you just have to figure out the solution, like those Lolo games.

737
00:48:44,331 --> 00:48:48,809
Speaker 1: As an old example from the NES days, if you figured out the solution, the execution was pretty easy.

738
00:48:49,150 --> 00:48:50,150
Speaker 0: Figuring out the solution was the hard part.

739
00:48:50,170 --> 00:48:52,190
Speaker 0: - Yeah, Lolo's a Sokoban, so it's all the same.

740
00:48:53,614 --> 00:48:54,769
Speaker 1: But I'm enjoying this game.

741
00:48:56,076 --> 00:48:56,670
Speaker 1: It's beautiful.

742
00:48:56,870 --> 00:48:58,350
